[Audio:start-up-tune:Start-up Tune]
Played by #R$AF88 each time a new game is started.
The music data is at #R$B20E.

#AUDIO0(start-up-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(StartUpTune))

[Audio:game-over-tune:Game Over Tune]
Played by #R$BA22 when the game is over, until a key is pressed.
The music data is at #R$B218.

#AUDIO0(game-over-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(GameOverTune))

[Audio:game-complete-tune:Game Complete Tune]
Played by #R$BAAB when the player has completed the game.
The music data is at #R$B239.

#AUDIO0(game-complete-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(GameCompleteTune))

[Audio:main-tune:Main Tune]
Played by #R$BD0C while the menu is shown, until a key is pressed.
The music data is at #R$B253.

#AUDIO0(main-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(MainTune))

[Audio:block-sound:Block Sound]
Played by #R$C4AA each time a block that can fall is handled.
Eight bursts of four cycles, one for each of the pitches of #R$B3FB.

#AUDIO0(block-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(BlockSound))

[Audio:sparkles-sound:Sparkles Sound]
Played by #R$BF2B and #R$C2A5 for each stage of the sparkles.
The eight stages of the death sparkles, one after the other.

#AUDIO0(sparkles-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(SparklesSound))

[Audio:appearing-sound:Appearing Sound]
Played by #R$BEFE for each stage of the sparkles that show the player appearing.
The seven stages, one after the other.

#AUDIO0(appearing-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(AppearingSound))

[Audio:bounce-sound:Bounce Sound]
Played by #R$B5FF, #R$B80F and #R$B865 when a ball or a fire bounces.
Four short bursts of a tone.

#AUDIO0(bounce-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(BounceSound))

[Audio:jump-sound:Jump Sound]
Played by #R$C948 when the player jumps.
A sweep of thirty-two single cycles.

#AUDIO0(jump-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(JumpSound))

[Audio:falling-sound:Falling Sound]
Played by #R$B683, #R$B7A9, #R$B865 and #R$C9A1 while an object falls.
The pitch comes from the height of the object, so here the object falls
through sixteen heights, one after the other.

#AUDIO0(falling-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(FallingSound))

[Audio:rising-sound:Rising Sound]
Played by #R$AFBA for each pass of the main loop while blocks are rising.
Six cycles of a tone.

#AUDIO0(rising-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(RisingSound))

[Audio:block-east-west-sound:Block East West Sound]
Played by #R$B6B9 and #R$B7ED while an object moves east or west.
The pitch comes from the X coordinate of the object, so here the object
moves through ten positions, one after the other.

#AUDIO0(block-east-west-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(BlockEastWestSound))

[Audio:block-north-south-sound:Block North South Sound]
Played by #R$B6B1 and #R$B80F while an object moves north or south.
The pitch comes from the Y coordinate of the object, so here the object
moves through ten positions, one after the other.

#AUDIO0(block-north-south-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(BlockNorthSouthSound))

[Audio:moving-sound:Moving Sound]
Played by #R$C232, #R$C5C8 and #R$C6BD while a special object, a ghost or a
portcullis moves.
The pitch comes from the three coordinates of the object, so here the
object rises through sixteen heights, one after the other.

#AUDIO0(moving-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(MovingSound))

[Audio:transform-sound:Transform Sound]
Played by #R$C337 while the player turns into a wulf or back into a human.
The pitch comes from the sprite of the transformation, so here the four
sprites are used three times each.

#AUDIO0(transform-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(TransformSound))

[Audio:explosion:Explosion]
Played by #R$C6BD when the portcullis comes to rest.
Sixteen short bursts of a tone, with pitches from a random place in the ROM.
The game picks the place at random, so here it is fixed.

#AUDIO0(explosion.wav)(#INCLUDE(Explosion))

[Audio:beep-sound:Beep Sound]
Played by #R$BD0C, #R$C00E and #R$C1AB when the player picks up or drops an
object, gets an extra life or changes the
control method on the menu.
Sixteen cycles of a low tone.

#AUDIO0(beep-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(BeepSound))

[Audio:pause-sound:Pause Sound]
Played by #R$D50E when the game is paused and when it carries on again.
Twenty-four cycles of a high tone.

#AUDIO0(pause-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(PauseSound))

[Audio:footstep-sound:Footstep Sound]
Played by #R$C89F and #R$C969 as the player walks.
The pitch comes from the position of the player, so here the player takes
eight steps along a line.

#AUDIO0(footstep-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(FootstepSound))

[Audio:guard-footstep-sound:Guard Footstep Sound]
Played by #R$B6F9 as a guard or the wizard walks.
The pitch comes from the position, so here the guard takes eight steps
along a line.

#AUDIO0(guard-footstep-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(GuardFootstepSound))
